{"requirements":[{"id":"R1","requirement":"Manage the supplied inventory-database and inventory-api programs as services on node1.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Both programs have valid, enabled systemd units and were directly observed running under systemd before and after reboot. The installed units and enablement persisted across the reboot.","evidence_ids":["cmd-34e343cc99254e2d","cmd-53964e648f7c4a59","cmd-7f3be8888b5347b3","cmd-421f599efade4419","cmd-dd6575c6ba254a68"]},{"id":"R2","requirement":"Ensure the API starts only after the database is ready.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The supplied database creates the readiness marker and the API requires it. From a marker-absent state, starting the API brought up the database first, completed its readiness check, and only then passed the API precheck. Post-reboot execution details and journal ordering independently confirm the same sequence.","evidence_ids":["cmd-1901e39453f843d4","cmd-53964e648f7c4a59","cmd-421f599efade4419","cmd-dd6575c6ba254a68"]}],"confidence":1,"operational_hygiene":{"score":1,"summary":"No unnecessary mutations were identified. Unit installation and enablement established the requested services; controlled stop/start and marker changes collected bounded dependency evidence and restored health; the reboot fulfilled the mandatory restart protocol. Read-only polling failures during reboot reflect expected connection loss. Final observations show no failed units, package damage, unexpected socket exposure, or abandoned temporary residue.","evidence_ids":["cmd-34e343cc99254e2d","cmd-53964e648f7c4a59","cmd-a71044702ad0418d","cmd-7f3be8888b5347b3","cmd-f11547834d124e5d","cmd-421f599efade4419","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets","global:after_executor:node1:package-health","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files"]},"overall_summary":"All material task outcomes are satisfied with direct behavioral evidence. The mandatory node-restart protocol is complete: a healthy pre-restart state and boot identity were captured, restart was acknowledged, the post-restart boot identity changed, and both services, readiness state, and processes recovered. The fixed lifecycle boot observations independently match those identities.","limitations":[]}
